From 545f8553df73bcab3807dec6660feac438740a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:02:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] dos: Add an off-by-default limit on open BEGIN_DIR
 streams per circuit

BEGIN_DIR returns before the stream creation defense, as the comment
there notes, so nothing bounds the BEGIN_DIR streams one circuit can
hold open (tor#41339). Each one costs a linked exit and directory
connection pair, which no connection limit counts and which can stay
open for minutes.

Add DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled, an AUTOBOOL whose "auto" default follows
the consensus parameter of the same name (default 0), and
DoSBeginDirMaxStreams (default 20). When enabled, a public relay
refuses a BEGIN_DIR stream on a circuit that already has that many open
directory streams, with END_STREAM_REASON_MISC as the stream defense
does.

From the client code, we expect stock clients to have a few directory
streams open on a circuit, and up to about 18 while bootstrapping from
a single directory guard. BEGIN_DIR cells over the limit are counted as
tor_relay_dos_total{type="begindir_over_max"} whether or not the limit
is enabled, so operators can check that before enabling it.

Unlike reusing DoSStreamCreation*, this leaves exit streams and the
existing options and counters unchanged.

Part of #41339.

