+[[DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled]] **DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Refuse a BEGIN_DIR stream on a circuit that already has
+    DoSBeginDirMaxStreams open directory streams. Clients treat a refused
+    stream as a failed directory request. Whatever this value, such streams
+    are counted on the MetricsPort. "auto" means use the consensus parameter.
+    If not defined in the consensus, the value is 0. (Default: auto)
+
+[[DoSBeginDirMaxStreams]] **DoSBeginDirMaxStreams** __NUM__::
+
+    The maximum number of open directory streams on a single circuit. See
+    DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled. If not defined or set to 0, it is controlled by a
+    consensus parameter. If not defined in the consensus, the value is 20.
+    (Default: 0)
+
 The following options are useful only for a exit relay.
 
